{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854830-kindred-in-toronto","id":854830,"title":"Kindred in Toronto?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-28T19:44:27-07:00","id":854830,"title":"Kindred in Toronto?","content":"So in the same vein of my Mage thread asking after Toronto, I want to put the question to players and storytellers of Vampire. What do you think the domain of Toronto looks like? Who is in charge? What weird things are going on? Is Toronto ever referenced in any Vampire books? Much obliged for your ideas!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T20:14:27-07:00","id":854845,"title":"","content":"Very little in the way of official material. The Bishop there is on the verge of discovering new Theban rituals.<br /> <br /> Sorry I don't have much to add, but I do love these bits of setting scattered throughout the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T20:15:05-07:00","id":854846,"title":"","content":"Not quite the answer you're looking for, but T'ranah actually had a bit of a write up in the Requiem Chronicler's Guide.<br /> <br /> To actually answer your question, I feel like there must be at least a few Nosferatu running the metro.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T21:03:53-07:00","id":854860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854830-kindred-in-toronto?p=854845#post854845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very little in the way of official material. The Bishop there is on the verge of discovering new Theban rituals.<br /> <br /> Sorry I don't have much to add, but I do love these bits of setting scattered throughout the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which book does that come from?<br /> <br /> That does give me some ideas, sweet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T21:08:16-07:00","id":854863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854830-kindred-in-toronto?p=854860#post854860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which book does that come from?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lancea Sanctum book, in the section about new rituals being discovered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T21:27:43-07:00","id":854867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854830-kindred-in-toronto?p=854846#post854846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite the answer you're looking for, but T'ranah actually had a bit of a write up in the Requiem Chronicler's Guide.<br /> <br /> To actually answer your question, I feel like there must be at least a few Nosferatu running the metro.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I remember reading this a long time ago. If nothing else, this material is good fodder for ideas.<br /> <br /> I was reading about Toronto's sewers the other day, it's like the place where the Bloodlines sewer level (UGH) could actually happen!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T22:06:34-07:00","id":854875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854830-kindred-in-toronto?p=854867#post854867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...it's like the place where the Bloodlines sewer level (UGH) could actually happen!</div> </div> </div> </div>DO NOT SPEAK OF THE SEWER LEVEL THAT ONLY GIVES IT POWER.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T23:39:05-07:00","id":854895,"title":"","content":"The cliche answer is that the city's run by Ventrue Invictus. More flavourful than that, though, any vampire of about two centuries of age probably remembers when this place was called York and was a part of Upper Canada.<br /> <br /> For that reason, I think you could have a lot of fun with making the vampires of Toronto a little microcosm of the old British Empire. Incorporate memories of imperial power, exoticism (and probably a heaping helping of orientalism, if you're up to trying to be tactful about it), and similar older notions into the story. The Victorian zeitgeist has not died in this part of the world.<br /> <br /> Some things you could incorporate (meaning you can use one, several, or all of these, but they aren't all expected to slot seamlessly together) include:<br /> <br /> -Vampires who have especially thick family lineages; only ever taking people of &quot;good breeding&quot; to join their undead bloodlines. Over time, such unholy inbreeding has produced some pretty noticeable and odd commonalities. Who knows? Perhaps a given Clan in the city consists entirely of direct relatives? Or consists entirely of a capital-B Bloodline?<br /> <br /> -Ordo Dracul mad scientists performing experiments in laboratories straight out of a Jules Verne novel: Kidnapping prostitutes or the homeless off the streets and subjecting them to twisted experiments to unveil more and more about what separates the quick and the dead.<br /> <br /> -Let's be honest, there's two other big strains of the British Empire that you might wanna throw in or stay the hell away from: Racism and slavery. Britain was astonishingly pro-abolitionism, being one of the few countries in the world to dedicate an entire naval squadron to actively combating the Atlantic Slave Trade, but it was still as racist as any other imperial power, justifying its tyrannical views as it saw fit. Those attitudes may linger, as may attitudes about sex and gender. Tread carefully using these, but they can be powerful if done right. Plus, if you want to give your players someone to beat mercilessly into the dirt, say they're a former slave trader who still carries the old prejudices. I doubt they'd feel bad curb-stomping that kind of person.<br /> <br /> -A corollary to the above: A fascination with all things foreign. Toronto is a city of immense diversity. The elders of it probably view it with a kind of fond paternalism. If there are old vampires from these cultures around too, though, then you might see something between fascination and bigotry flaring between them.<br /> <br /> -The Lancea could be an exceptionally sharp moralizing force, with Jack the Ripper as something of a patron saint; a terror that strikes fear into those of &quot;low moral character&quot; is pretty much the perfect symbol of those sorts of monsters.<br /> <br /> -The Carthian Movement and Daevas probably fit in more with the modern city, as do the Nosferatu. Toronto's got a pretty vibrant night life and an equally vibrant political side. The Carthians probably get dismissed as &quot;the rabble&quot; by the old gentry, and perhaps even take to using the clothing and symbols of anarchists and similar troublemakers of yesteryear to mock their elders.<br /> <br /> I could go on but I think you get the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T15:26:55-07:00","id":856744,"title":"","content":"Here is my plan for Toronto.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking a Circle of the Crone Princess, Viod Style of Cruac, who sees herself as a modern day Emperor Julian the Philospher, whose right hand man is a Lancea Sanctum Belialist Heretic who believes Belial is Lonigus's Beast, and its only through Belial (pledge with the worthless) that a Vampire can achieve salvation.<br /> <br /> This Belialist has been declared Archbishop of Toronto pissing off the Majority of Sactum in the City, but none dare challenge the combined power of the local Crone and Sanctum the Heretics.<br /> <br /> The Catharium are satisified with experimenting with the students of Ryerson University, so in exchange for semiautomy on Campus and surrounding area, they've given their support to the Princess.<br /> <br /> The Invictus used to rule Toronto from the towering heights of Bay Street, but after a massive set back, they were betrayed by the mainstream Lanca Sanctum with whom they fought a brief war, which ended with an alliance of Crone and Belialists seizing power in a sudden and brutal move.<br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul have been bought off by being granted greater freedom to explore blood magic experiments on humans then the Invictus allowed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T20:32:27-07:00","id":856906,"title":"","content":"The model I've currently got scooped some material from the Chronicler's guide, with a British aristocratic family &amp; Ventrue Lineage that's been involved with the Invictus through the centuries is in charge, with its patriarch as the Lord Prince of Toronto. Thusfar the concept is less that it's an Invictus city and more that its the Lord Prince's city. The Invictus don't have numbers, but the mainstream is very savvy on technology and surveillance, while the core is traditional blue blooded First Estaters.<br /> <br /> Prior to the Lord Prince, Toronto had passed hands between a couple of Kindred groups, but thanks to an alliance brokered between the Sanctified and the Ordo Dracul, the Lord Prince won out. I'm imagining this is an alliance between influential individuals rather than an alliance between factions, y'know?<br /> <br /> I know it's a bit unexciting, but I'm very open to thoughts on spicing it up. I've made my settings in the past highly factionalized, and I'm kind of hoping with this one to make it more about the personalities that inhabit each faction rather than open warfare between the Sanctified and the Crone kind of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T14:57:11-07:00","id":857303,"title":"","content":"So, thinking on the Prince some more, I'm definitely feeling like he has a &quot;Uneasy lies the head that wears a crown.&quot; kind of thing going on. In life, he was a ruthless businessman who had convinced himself that everything he was doing was for the benefit of his family and of the city. Then, towards the end of his life, before he gets embraced, mortality looms and he has the kind of crisis of conscience that afflicted a lot of the robber barons of the 19th century, maybe, though his string of failures left him with little finance to give. Then his nephew Benedict shows up bearing one of the family's old secrets, and he's made immortal. I don't think he stopped feeling that sense of guilt over what he'd done, but how would that change? How would he react to the commandments of the Elder that really lead the family (Who is now, either dead or in torpor, presumably.)<br /> <br /> And of course, thinking about Benedict, I'm imagining he's a very power hungry, savvy one, and when he was finally Embraced, he became the Lord Prince's right hand man. I'm thinking, what if he's the real power behind the throne here?<br /> <br /> For reference, I'm discussing the background of the fictional D'Arcy family (who I've currently renamed the Blackwood family, after the British aristocratic family) which is described in the <i>Requiem Chronicler's Guide</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adapted from The Requiem Chronicler's Guide</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The </span></span>Blackwood<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> family legacy spreads out from its home, the magnificent castle of Casa Loma that looms over Toronto, to dominate the All-Night Society. Sir Henry </span></span>Blackwood<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, born in Upper Canada in 1859 to British parents, military hero of the Queen\u2019s Own Rifles, a businessman with a Midas touch, built his own castle in 1911.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As soon as the castle was completed in 1914, a curse seemed to fall upon the family. First, his wife, Lady Mary </span></span>Blackwood<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, fell victim to a wasting disease, which confined her to a wheelchair. Then, </span></span>Blackwood'<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">s fortunes began to collapse. He went further into debt to expand his holdings, and new investments failed to turn profit. A popular myth of the era suggested that </span></span>Blackwood<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2019s earlier successes were achieved through a deal of a nefarious sort, and that it was time for his backers to collect their due.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sir Henry appeared to lose everything. He sold the estate, and the family moved to their farm in 1924. Shortly after, Mary died. Casa Loma sat vacant, and was taken over by the city in 1933 in lieu of back taxes. It was to be reopened as a tourist attraction in the late 1930s, but in the year of Sir Henry\u2019s death a distant relative, Benedict </span></span>Blackwood<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, swept in and bought it back into the family.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The true history of the family is known only to its members. Benedict not only restored the family\u2019s fortune, but returned Sir Henry and Mary to Casa Loma. Reportedly dead, they continued to exist as Kindred. When the time was right, and the next generation was prepared to take over the family interests, Sir Henry Embraced Benedict. Since then the </span></span>Blackwood<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> continue to subtly influence the city. </span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 04-02-2016, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:02:35-07:00","id":857418,"title":"","content":"I wish I can ask about borrowing some of these ideas for my Las Vegas campaign, but it has a completely different history with a different climate and an atmosphere that I don't think I can replicate as well as in Toronto. I do love these ideas however. Las Vegas has a significantly large night life much like Toronto so I figured I can still look at this page for inspiration. Is that okay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11528-dangerus-muyoko-project","name":"Dangerus-Muyoko-Project","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:31:07-07:00","id":857435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dangerus-Muyoko-Project</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854830-kindred-in-toronto?p=857418#post857418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish I can ask about borrowing some of these ideas for my Las Vegas campaign, but it has a completely different history with a different climate and an atmosphere that I don't think I can replicate as well as in Toronto. I do love these ideas however. Las Vegas has a significantly large night life much like Toronto so I figured I can still look at this page for inspiration. Is that okay?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pfft, absolutely! The whole point is for us to be inspired and inspire in turn, though I actually do have some Las Vegas material if you want to look at that too. PM me if you'd like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:32:33-07:00","id":857436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854830-kindred-in-toronto?p=857435#post857435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Pfft, absolutely! The whole point is for us to be inspired and inspire in turn, though I actually do have some Las Vegas material if you want to look at that too. PM me if you'd like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I may update my own topic on Las Vegas for later on, but this would be fantastic that I get feedback from someone outside my older brother and my current ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11528,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11528-dangerus-muyoko-project","user":"Dangerus-Muyoko-Project","date":". 04-01-2016, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11528-dangerus-muyoko-project","name":"Dangerus-Muyoko-Project","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:08:55-07:00","id":857461,"title":"","content":"Well since you've asked I figured I'd throw in my thoughts having run/played in a few Vampire games in Toronto. The two things of note we did were these.<br /> <br /> Firstly as you mentioned in your Mage thread, Toronto is a very multicultural city. We used this as a good excuse to have a wide variety of bloodlines in it from all cultures. Toronto being the melting pot it is made even some of the more obscure ones showing up seem reasonable<br /> <br /> Second politically we went with an uneasy peace between the various Covenants within the city. Carthians and Invictus heavily outnumber the other covenants and are roughly evenly matched. The Carthians have used this influence to push for the city to be run by council rather than a princedom as it were. The priscus for each clan has a seat, as do the leaders of each covenant. The tiebreaker is held by an elected chancellor. Thereby ensuring decisions are made fairly and by vote. Of course the fact that the elected chancellor also happens to lead the Invictus and be the priscus for the Daeva does somewhat explain why she was willing to agree to such a system.<br /> <br /> Anyways just figured I'd post cause Toronto tends to be our group's default city <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2989-violetdea","name":"violetdea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T23:11:08-07:00","id":857527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854830-kindred-in-toronto?p=854875#post854875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> DO NOT SPEAK OF THE SEWER LEVEL THAT ONLY GIVES IT POWER.</div> </div> </div> </div>This totally sounds like it could be a Crash Bandicoot level more than a VTMB thing. Although, I doubt most Kindred would be great at resisting electric eels zapping the water all too well (basically, if you're a Gangrel Mara needing to feed, you're doomed unless you're a low Blood Potency and want to be on Eel cleanup duty). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854830-kindred-in-toronto?p=854845#post854845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very little in the way of official material. The Bishop there is on the verge of discovering new Theban rituals.<br /> <br /> Sorry I don't have much to add, but I do love these bits of setting scattered throughout the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the Bishop's discovery of Theban rituals would likely influence the province, unless the Sanctified simply don't have the numbers to back up the sheer power of these new Theban discoveries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11527-hakamichi-kurloz-sir","name":"Hakamichi Kurloz, Sir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T23:29:12-07:00","id":857533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakamichi Kurloz, Sir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854830-kindred-in-toronto?p=857527#post857527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the Bishop's discovery of Theban rituals would likely influence the province, unless the Sanctified simply don't have the numbers to back up the sheer power of these new Theban discoveries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was thinking about what the character of this Bishop might be, as I think they're the one that is part of the Lord Prince's little clique. If I recall correctly, the Bishop's discovery is in the 90's, so maybe it has caused them to start drifting apart, if there was something more than just new rituals there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}